    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.surround\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12.x\n\n### Description\n\nIn the following Lua code\n\n```lua\nfoo(bar(a, b, c))\n```\n\nwhen placing the cursor on \"bar\", changing or deleting the call (`sd`, `sr`) does nothing. It works fine on \"foo\".\n\nThis doesn't seem to be the problem with [queries](https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter-textobjects/blob/851e865342e5a4cb1ae23d31caf6e991e1c99f1e/queries/lua/textobjects.scm#L5-L17), I tested all of them in `:EditQuery` and they highlight inner/outer parts of the calls correctly.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n```lua\n-- Clone latest 'mini.nvim' (requires Git CLI installed)\nvim.cmd('echo \"Installing `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\nlocal mini_path = vim.fn.stdpath('data') .. '/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim'\nlocal clone_cmd = { 'git', 'clone', '--depth=1', 'https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim', mini_path }\nvim.fn.system(clone_cmd)\nvim.cmd('echo \"`mini.nvim` is installed\" | redraw')\n\n-- Make sure 'mini.nvim' is available\nvim.cmd('packadd mini.nvim')\nrequire('mini.deps').setup()\n\n-- Add extra setup steps needed to reproduce the behavior\n-- Use `MiniDeps.add('user/repo')` to install another plugin from GitHub\nMiniDeps.add({\n    source = 'nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter',\n    checkout = 'main',\n})\nMiniDeps.add({\n    source = 'nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter-textobjects',\n    checkout = 'main',\n})\n\nlocal surround = require \"mini.surround\"\nlocal ts_input = surround.gen_spec.input.treesitter\n\nrequire(\"mini.surround\").setup {\n    custom_surroundings = {\n        C = {\n            input = ts_input { outer = \"@call.outer\", inner = \"@call.inner\" },\n            output = function()\n                local fun_name = surround.user_input \"Function name\"\n                if fun_name == nil then return nil end\n                return { left = fun_name .. \"(\", right = \")\" }\n            end,\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n-- After installation:\n-- :lua require(\"nvim-treesitter\").install(\"lua\")\n```",
