        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue! I can reproduce.\n\nIt is an issue with how 'mini.surround' pairs outer capture matches with inner capture matches. It currently searches the biggest inner match that is within given outer match, but fails to account for the fact that some inner match can be equal to the given outer match. Like in this case: `bar(a, b, c)` is both a `@call.outer` match and `@call.innner` match (for `foo(...)`). Luckily the fix should be straightforward, I'll get to it.",
